== 1. Claude Code fixes the bug (no chloe MCP, no memory_save) ==
All 3 tests pass now.

**Root cause:** `page_count` used floor division (`//`), which drops a partial last page, so 21 items at 10 per page gave 2 pages and 3 items gave 0. I changed it to ceiling division, `-(-total_items // per_page)`.

I didn't check `per_page == 0` or negative inputs. The function still raises `ZeroDivisionError` on zero, as it did before.
OK
